<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # 3 – Lesson # 3</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 3</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Speaking</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 6th Grade (CEFR: A2.1)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Our Amazing Community</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> This Is My Amazing Community.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Speaking: productive: Describe a tradition or celebration. interactive: Exchange opinions about familiar topics.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Speaking: Can describe a community tradition using simple language and time expressions (e.g., 'In our town, we have a music festival every year, like the Panama Jazz Festival. It takes place in January.' 'La Mejorana Festival happens in Guararé, Los Santos Province, usually in September.'). Can exchange opinions on community topics (e.g., 'I like our park. Do you?'). Can share information about community events (e.g., 'What time is the music festival?' 'It begins at 2:00 p.m.').</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
        <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; color: #1a5276; width: 30%;">Stage & Description</th>
        <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; color: #1a5276; width: 50%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
        <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; color: #1a5276; width: 20%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling, and Clarification to activate prior knowledge and introduce the lesson's focus.</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher shows pictures of different community events and traditions from Panama (e.g., a "Diablicos Sucios" dance, a "pollera" parade, a local food market, a music festival like the Panama Jazz Festival). Students quickly identify them by saying the name or a related word in English. The teacher asks, "What do you see?" "What is this event?" "Do you like it?" to elicit simple responses.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models describing one of the events using target language. For example: "This is a <b>traditional</b> parade. It happens in my <b>neighborhood every year</b>. People <b>gather</b> at the <b>park before</b> it starts. They <b>celebrate</b> our culture. I like it very much." The teacher emphasizes stress in 'neighborhood' and clearly pronounces short /ʊ/ in 'cook' (if mentioning food) and long /uː/ in 'school' (if relevant to the community). The teacher models question formation: "What do people do at the festival?" and "When does it happen?"</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Does the parade happen every day or every year?" (Checks 'every year' and time expressions.)</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Do people gather alone or together?" (Checks 'gather' and community concept.)</li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
        </td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content through an authentic text, dialogue, or audio/visual material.</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> Short audio dialogue between two children (Maria and Carlos) discussing a local community festival, potentially the "Festival de La Mejorana."</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Dialogue Excerpt:</b></p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Maria: "Our <b>community</b> has a great <b>festival</b> each year, like the La Mejorana Festival! It usually happens in September. Do you know it?"</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Carlos: "Oh, yes! I've heard about it. My family <b>visits</b> Guararé <b>last year</b> for it. What do people usually do?"</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Maria: "Well, people <b>gather</b> to watch folk dances and listen to <b>musicians</b>. They also <b>cook delicious food</b> at the <b>market</b>. I think it's very <b>engaging</b>!"</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Carlos: "That sounds fun! What delicious food do people <b>cook</b> at the <b>market</b>? I really like the atmosphere. I like our <b>park</b> too. Do you?"</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Maria: "Yes, I like our park. People usually <b>share</b> food and stories. My aunt is a <b>vendor</b> there. She has worked there for ten years."</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Listening for specific information to understand descriptions of community traditions and opinions.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist question:</b> "What are Maria and Carlos talking about?" (Expected answer: A community festival / La Mejorana Festival.)</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"The festival happens every month." (False)</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Carlos' family visited Guararé last year." (True)</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Maria's aunt is a teacher." (False)</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10 min</p>
        </td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Controlled and semi-controlled activities focusing on accuracy in Speaking.</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Present simple and past simple with time expressions, forming questions in present simple, present perfect tense, and vocabulary related to community roles, events, and opinions. Pronunciation of compound nouns (e.g., 'music festival', 'police officer') and short/long vowel sounds (/ʊ/ in 'cook', /uː/ in 'school').</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled practice (Sentence Completion & Choral Repetition):</b> The teacher provides sentence frames and prompts. Students complete sentences aloud, focusing on correct grammar and vocabulary. The class then repeats phrases chorally, focusing on pronunciation.
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Our community has a _______ (festival / market) _______ (every year / last month)."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"People _______ (cook / build) _______ (delicious / fresh) food there."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"My neighbor is a _______ (carpenter / musician). He _______ (builds / plays) things." (Focus on 'neighbor' stress).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I _______ (have worked / worked) as a _______ (teacher / farmer) for _______ (five years / yesterday)."</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled (Question and Answer Chain):</b> Students work in pairs. Teacher provides question prompts, and students ask and answer using the target structures. Teacher monitors for correct question formation and use of time expressions.
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Prompt 1: "What / people / cook / market?" (Student A: "What delicious food do people cook at the market?" Student B: "They cook tasty empanadas.")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Prompt 2: "When / your community / celebrate / main event?" (Student A: "When does your community celebrate its main event?" Student B: "Our community celebrates its main event in December, before Christmas.")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Prompt 3: "How long / your teacher / work / here?" (Student A: "How long has your teacher worked here?" Student B: "She has worked here for five years.")</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair Interaction (Role-Play with Dialogue Frames):</b> Students work in pairs. Each pair receives a dialogue frame with gaps, based on the Presentation stage dialogue. They fill the gaps with their own information about a community event or tradition.
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student A: "Our <b>community</b> has a great _______ (e.g., music festival) every year, like the _______ (e.g., Panama Jazz Festival)! It takes place in _______ (e.g., January). Do you know it?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student B: "Oh, yes! I've heard about it. My family _______ (visited / enjoyed) it _______ (last year / last month). What do people usually do?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student A: "People _______ (gather / meet) to watch _______ (traditional / beautiful) dances and listen to _______ (musicians / artists). They also _______ (share / enjoy) _______ (sweet / fresh) fruits."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student B: "That sounds fun! I like our _______ (park / library). Do you?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student A: "Yes, I like our _______ (park / school). My _______ (neighbor / family member) is a _______ (vendor / police officer) there. He/She has worked there for _______ (number) years."</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15 min</p>
        </td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students use the language in a realistic scenario, focusing on fluency and interaction.</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> "Community News Report" - Students work in pairs to create and present a short, interactive dialogue simulating a news report about a community tradition or event.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students choose a specific community event or tradition (real or imagined) from their town or another part of Panama (e.g., the "La Mejorana Festival," "Carnavales," or a local market event).</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">One student acts as the "reporter" and the other as a "community member" or "organizer."</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">They prepare a short dialogue (3-5 exchanges) to inform the "audience" about the event. They need to include:
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What the event is (e.g., "Our <b>community</b> has a _______ <b>festival</b>...")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">When it happens (using time expressions like 'every year', 'in January', 'last month').</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What people do there (e.g., 'people <b>gather</b>', 'they <b>cook delicious food</b>', 'they <b>enjoy</b> music').</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">An opinion about the event (e.g., 'I like it because it is very <b>welcoming</b>').</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">At least one question about community roles or experiences (e.g., "What does your <b>neighbor</b> do at this event?" "How long has your <b>artist</b> friend worked here?").</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Pairs practice their dialogue, focusing on fluent delivery, clear pronunciation (e.g., 'neighborhood' stress, /ʊ/ vs /uː/ sounds), and natural interaction.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Selected pairs perform their "news report" for the class.</li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10 min</p>
        </td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment to check learning and student self-reflection.</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist for pairs during the "Community News Report."</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students perform their "Community News Report" dialogue.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher Checklist):</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Intelligible pronunciation (e.g., correct stress in compound nouns, clear vowel sounds).</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use of at least 5 target vocabulary words (e.g., <i>community, festival, gather, delicious, traditional, vendor</i>).</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct use of present simple to describe traditions and past simple for past experiences.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Asks and answers questions effectively (e.g., "What delicious food do people cook at the market?").</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Exchanges opinions about familiar topics (e.g., "I like our park. Do you?").</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Task completion: Successfully described a community event.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Collaboration and interaction within the pair.</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students write down their answers to the following questions before leaving:</p>
            <ul>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was one new thing you learned to say about your community today?"</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of talking about community events was easy for you? What was difficult?"</li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">7-8 min</p>
        </td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Teacher and student reflection on the lesson and connection to future learning.</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt (oral or written):</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What role do you think you play in your community? Share with your partner one way you can help."</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Can you now describe a community tradition or celebration to a friend?"</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">What worked well in this speaking lesson? The pair work with dialogue frames helped students build confidence using the structures. The "Community News Report" was engaging and allowed for creative use of language. What challenges did students face? Some students struggled with consistently forming questions in the present simple and differentiating between present simple and past simple for different time expressions. Pronunciation of compound nouns like 'neighborhood' and 'music festival' will require continued practice. Adjustments needed for next lesson: Provide more explicit drills or quick checks on question formation. Incorporate a warm-up that reviews time expressions more directly. Create sentence starters for question formation as a scaffold.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In Lesson 4, students will use the vocabulary and grammatical structures practiced today to write a short paragraph describing a community tradition or event, moving from oral production to written composition.</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">3-5 min</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>